document.querySelector('#guide').innerHTML=`
 <p class="eyebrow">PONGFETCH / BUILD GUIDE</p><h1 class="page-title">A little making.<br>A lot of playing.</h1><p class="lead">From a flat print to a ball picker. Work through the steps at your own pace.</p>
 <div class="guide-layout"><aside class="guide-sidebar"><h2>Before you start</h2><ul class="parts-list"><li><span>01</span>Printed frame with integrated latches</li><li><span>02</span>Clamp cap + collet</li><li><span>03</span>Fine mesh net</li><li><span>04</span>PVC pipe matched to the socket</li><li><span>05</span>Table tennis balls for a first try</li></ul><p class="aside-note">Use Bambu PETG Basic for the printed parts. Measure your pipe before printing; the current collet has a nominal 21.74 mm bore.</p><a class="button primary" href="#downloads">Get the files ↓</a><div class="progress-wrap"><label for="build-progress" id="progress-label">0 of 5 steps complete</label><progress id="build-progress" max="5" value="0"></progress><button type="button" class="quiet-button" id="reset-progress">Reset progress</button></div></aside>
 <div class="steps">
 <details class="step" open><summary><span class="step-number">01</span><span>Choose your print files<small>Start with the version notes.</small></span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="step-body"><p>The current frame, cap and collet have been printed and confirmed usable. Rev 3.0 adds flush two-colour lettering to the four front and rear latches.</p><p>Use the current Rev 3.0 files and re-slice for your own printer. The new lettering has been checked in the slicer; its colour finish still awaits a physical print.</p><a class="text-link" href="#downloads">Get the files ↗</a><label class="step-check"><input type="checkbox" data-step="0"> I have chosen my files.</label></div></details>
 <details class="step"><summary><span class="step-number">02</span><span>Print &amp; release<small>Keep the small moving parts free.</small></span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="step-body"><p>The latest frame project saves a 0.20 mm first layer and 4 walls. The small-parts project also retains the latest saved 4 walls and 0.20 mm layers. Keep each project's orientation and check the settings for your printer.</p><img class="guide-image" src="assets/first-layer.webp" width="1200" height="800" alt="CAD close-up of the frame's three temporary internal ties at a latch" loading="lazy"><p>Let the print cool. For the internal-tie version, release the three small ties at each latch one at a time from the print-bed side. Check that each tab can press and spring back before closing it.</p><p class="note">Only break the small internal ties. The flush lettering is permanent and is included in the Rev 3.0 frame 3MF.</p><label class="step-check"><input type="checkbox" data-step="1"> The parts are printed and released.</label></div></details>
 <details class="step"><summary><span class="step-number">03</span><span>Fit the net<small>In the channels, loose at the corners.</small></span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="step-body"><img class="product-front guide-front" src="assets/sunshine-front.webp" width="2100" height="650" alt="Net running in the straight-edge channel between the two front latches, with extra mesh at the corners" loading="lazy"><p>Spread the net across the frame and leave enough mesh above it to hold the balls. On each straight edge, route the net through the continuous channel between the two latches.</p><p>Allow a little extra mesh at the corners. Fold the latches up 90° and close them over the net, checking that the mesh is seated in the channel and the latches engage.</p><label class="step-check"><input type="checkbox" data-step="2"> The net is seated and the latches are closed.</label></div></details>
 <details class="step"><summary><span class="step-number">04</span><span>Add the handle<small>A simple white PVC pipe.</small></span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="step-body"><p>Slide the cap and collet onto the PVC pipe. Insert the pipe fully into the socket. For the skirted collet, seat the locating skirt in the socket and keep its flange flat against the socket rim.</p><p>Hand-tighten the cap until the pipe no longer slips. Check the fit and make sure the cap can be loosened again.</p><label class="step-check"><input type="checkbox" data-step="3"> The handle is fitted and secure.</label></div></details>
 <details class="step"><summary><span class="step-number">05</span><span>Pick. Play.<small>Give it a gentle first try.</small></span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="step-body"><p>Start with a few balls on a flat floor. Place the frame over them and press down gently so they pass through the fins into the net.</p><p>Lift the picker and check that the balls stay inside, the net stays in its channels and the handle does not slip. Adjust the assembly if needed before filling it further.</p><label class="step-check"><input type="checkbox" data-step="4"> Ready for the next rally.</label></div></details>
 </div></div>`;

document.querySelector('#downloads').innerHTML=`
 <div class="download-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PONGFETCH / DOWNLOADS / REV 3.0</p><h1 class="page-title">Ready. Set.<br>Make.</h1><p class="lead">Three printed parts. Pick the files that fit your workflow, and build your own PongFetch.</p><a class="license-inline" href="#license">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 <span>Personal &amp; noncommercial use ↗</span></a></div><div class="download-feature"><p class="eyebrow">ONE PICKER. YOUR WAY.</p><img class="product-front" src="assets/sunshine-front.webp" width="2100" height="650" alt="PongFetch front latches and net"><span class="release-stamp">rev <strong>3.0</strong></span><p>Frame + cap + collet</p><a class="button primary" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Maker_Bundle.zip" download>Get everything ↓</a><small data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Maker_Bundle.zip"></small></div></div>
 <div class="format-guide" aria-label="Choose a file format"><div><span>01 / READY TO SLICE</span><h2>3MF</h2><p>Saved parts, colours and settings.<br>Re-slice for your own printer.</p></div><div><span>02 / YOUR OWN SETUP</span><h2>STL</h2><p>Single-colour geometry.<br>Choose your own slicer settings.</p></div><div><span>03 / MAKE A CHANGE</span><h2>Source</h2><p>Editable OpenSCAD design.<br>Adjust dimensions and lettering.</p></div></div>
 <div class="downloads-toolbar"><h2>The print files</h2><div class="file-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter download groups"><button type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button><button type="button" data-filter="frame" aria-pressed="false">Frame</button><button type="button" data-filter="parts" aria-pressed="false">Cap &amp; collet</button><button type="button" data-filter="source" aria-pressed="false">Source</button></div></div>
 <div class="download-rows">
 <article class="download-row" data-category="frame"><span class="row-number">01</span><div class="row-description"><p class="eyebrow">REV 3.0 / FRAME</p><h2>The frame.</h2><p>The frame, socket and eight folding latches, printed together. Choose 3MF for the flush two-colour lettering.</p><p class="file-meta">Mechanism print-confirmed · New lettering finish awaits a print</p></div><div class="download-options"><a class="download-option recommended" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Frame.3mf" download><span><strong>Frame · 3MF</strong><small>Two-colour lettering included <b data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Frame.3mf"></b></small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="download-option" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Frame.stl" download><span><strong>Frame · STL</strong><small>Single-colour solid <b data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Frame.stl"></b></small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="option-note">STL has no colour assignments. Flush colour lettering is not visible in the single-solid mesh.</p></div></article>
 <article class="download-row" data-category="parts"><span class="row-number">02</span><div class="row-description"><p class="eyebrow">REV 3.0 / HANDLE PARTS</p><h2>Cap &amp; collet.</h2><p>The screw-on cap and six-finger collet secure the PVC handle. Print both together, or download each part separately.</p><p class="file-meta">Print &amp; fit confirmed · Two separate printed parts</p></div><div class="download-options"><a class="download-option recommended" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Handle_Parts.3mf" download><span><strong>Cap + collet · 3MF</strong><small>One of each, saved orientation <b data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Handle_Parts.3mf"></b></small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><div class="split-downloads"><a class="download-option" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Cap.stl" download><span><strong>Cap · STL</strong><small data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Cap.stl"></small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="download-option" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Collet.stl" download><span><strong>Collet · STL</strong><small data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Collet.stl"></small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div></article>
 <article class="download-row source-row" data-category="source"><span class="row-number">03</span><div class="row-description"><p class="eyebrow">REV 3.0 / EDITABLE DESIGN</p><h2>Your next idea.</h2><p>The four OpenSCAD design files, build notes and license. Change the design for noncommercial use; share your remixes under the same license.</p><p class="file-meta">Requires OpenSCAD + BOSL2 · Font files not included</p></div><div class="download-options"><a class="download-option recommended" href="downloads/PongFetch_Rev3_Design_Source.zip" download><span><strong>Design source · ZIP</strong><small>SCAD + notes + license <b data-file-size="PongFetch_Rev3_Design_Source.zip"></b></small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Tia-Lin/PongFetch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View project on GitHub ↗</a><p class="option-note">Private repository · source not yet uploaded. Download the editable design using the ZIP above.</p></div></article>
 </div><p id="file-count" class="file-count" aria-live="polite">3 download groups</p>
 <div class="download-bottom"><div><p class="eyebrow">KEEP THE GOOD IDEAS MOVING</p><h2>Print. Remix.<br>Share alike.</h2><p>Personal printing is welcome. Commercial use needs separate permission. When you share an adaptation, credit PongFetch, note your changes and follow the ShareAlike terms.</p><a class="text-link" href="#license">Understand the license ↗</a></div><div><h3>Before you hit print</h3><p>Re-slice every 3MF for your machine and loaded filament. The website palette changes the preview; set your print colours in your slicer.</p><p>We encourage sharing editable source with a remix. It is a community request, not an extra license requirement.</p><a class="text-link" href="downloads/PongFetch_Print_Notes.txt" download>Printing &amp; assembly notes ↓</a></div></div>`;

